CORE
explicit_x_merged_writes.sv
--top main --bound 3
^\[main\.p_known\] .*: PROVED up to bound 3$
^\[main\.p_hold\] .*: PROVED up to bound 3$
^\[main\.r_x_free0\] .*: REFUTED$
^\[main\.r_x_free1\] .*: REFUTED$
^\[main\.p_two_state\] .*: PROVED up to bound 3$
^\[main\.p_same\] .*: PROVED up to bound 3$
^\[main\.r_independent\] .*: REFUTED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
--
64 guarded bit writes with explicit x in one always construct. The commit
samples the x bits of the four-state target: one value per write, read
consistently, independent between bits; the two-state target reads 0.
